{"author":{"id":"dec876858d28babbadcead4137861bf586626b8518cbce9c5f4fc52ac3b424b8"},"ops":[{"type":3,"timestamp":1791621236,"nonce":"RIbd/cKR/Ndk1XZYZkiPT5AbrAw=","message":"Router page-transition exit playback landed in 098a7fb8 (outlet) with absolute_when in d7e3c7f9 and a tab-exit test in 790324f0.\n\nHow: a page with a PageTransition gets a stable-keyed motion per navigation (router-page-\u003crouter\u003e-\u003cversion\u003e), so MotionHandle::exit can address it. The outlet keeps the old page mounted as a leaving row, made absolute (Div::absolute_when, per-row signal set by start) so the new page is not pushed aside, until the motion's exit is no longer animating. The runner's end_stable_motion_frame drops each page's motion state once the page is gone (a test checks motions do not pile up over 12 navigations); both windowed.rs and web.rs run it.\n\nVerified headless, not in a window: tests/outlet_exit.rs (router) and tests/tabs_exit.rs (cn) drive a RenderState through the runner's frame order (process queued exits, sync the motion store, drain property updates, motion frame bookkeeping, tick) in 16ms steps; the old page stays out of flow and goes after about 200ms, a zero-length exit goes at once, and mutations (exit never started, page left in flow, done always true) each fail them. MotionHandle::exit is only processed on the next render frame, which is why done is first asked one frame after start.\n\nLimit: the leaving page is positioned at the start of the outlet's content box, not where it was. In a centered outlet whose pages differ in width the old page can shift as it fades. Fixing that would need the old page's bounds at the moment it starts to leave.","files":null}]}